The search as the frontend sees it, and the kept search (mu-engine/patches/net-0001; Melee-NX-NetPlay's patches/net-0005 and
net-0010, as melee-unlocked does it in its slippi_online.cpp search_away / kept_search):
- search_info(): the search's state, mode, the connect code searched for, the locked-in fighter, whether the others locked in and
  the first other player's pick, elapsed time, error and opponent, for the frontend's search module (play while you search,
  "Search again?", the warm-up room and its sparring partner).
- keep_search(): a kept search goes on through the game's own cleanup commands while the player plays offline (the frontend
  decides when; nothing changes unless the player chose it). end_kept_search() ends it.
- frame_trace(): the last online frame's wait, time sync halt or advance and time sync offset (the network overlay).
Read only on the wire: nothing sent changes. Applied by ../net_sources.sh to a copy of port/runtime/hle; port/ is unchanged.

